    "body": "I don't like all the manual state management, but I suppose the performance speed-up is worth it.\r\n\r\nBut to at least avoid the management of two path buffers, I would prefer to return a `PathBuf` and `pop()` it once for iteration (This may need to be `loop if` pseudo `do while`-loop to handle the initial level, but ideally that would re-use the cwd scan anyway)\r\n```suggestion\r\n        let mut dir = PathBuf::with_capacity(path.as_os_str().len() + 15);\r\n        dir.push(self.path);\r\n        while dir.pop() {\r\n```\r\n\r\nFWIW mimalloc also manages similar performance without code changes.",
